--- !u!114 &999943425
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 999943423}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 6ed1154995f8e334cabbeb5799cf4642, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::PhysicsLab.Lab.GuideBoard
  pages:
  - title: <b>LAB BENCH</b>
    body: 'Goal: the ring sits round the centre post, still.


      <color=#FFD54F><b>Steps</b></color><color=#9AA7B5>  (your step shows on the left)</color>

      1  Setup: the spring scale reads 0 N.

      2  Configure masses: clamp pulleys, hang masses.

      3  Connect scale: hook it on and pull.

      4  Equilibrium: ring centred and still.

      5  Record: press Record, then Next step.'
  - title: <b>THE FOUR CASES</b>
    body: '<color=#FFD54F><b>Do A, B, C and D</b></color>

      <color=#9AA7B5>Any pulley may take any row of the case.</color>

      A<pos=6%><size=85%>200 g at 30 deg</size><pos=35%><size=85%>200 g at 120 deg</size>

      B<pos=6%><size=85%>200 g at 30 deg</size><pos=35%><size=85%>150 g at 80 deg</size>

      C<pos=6%><size=85%>200 g at 5 deg</size><pos=35%><size=85%>150 g at 95 deg</size>

      D<pos=6%><size=85%>100 g at 40 deg</size><pos=35%><size=85%>200 g at 100 deg</size><pos=64%><size=85%>300 g at 235 deg</size>


      <color=#9AA7B5>150 g = 100 g + 50 g.   300 g = 200 g + 100 g.</color>

      <color=#9AA7B5>Cases A to C use two pulleys. Case D uses three.</color>'
  - title: <b>SET UP A CASE</b>
    body: 'Press Next step. The left screen shows

      Configure masses (n to fix). n must reach 0.

      <color=#FFD54F><b>Clamp a pulley</b></color>

      Let go within 10 cm of the spot for its angle.

      It counts if it is within 2 degrees.

      <color=#FFD54F><b>Hang the masses</b></color>

      Hang them on the loop under that pulley.

      <color=#9AA7B5>Cases A to C: leave Pulley 3 where it is.</color>'
  - title: <b>CONNECT THE SCALE</b>
    body: 'Press Next step.

      Grab the spring scale. Pull it away from the ring.

      Keep pulling until the ring sits on the post

      and stays still. The step then shows (done).

      <color=#9AA7B5>The scale reads only while you hold it.</color>

      <color=#9AA7B5>Let go and the reading goes to 0 N.</color>

      <color=#FFD54F><b>Stuck?</b></color>

      Ask the assistant on the right screen.'
  - title: <b>RECORD AND REPEAT</b>
    body: 'Press Record while the ring is still.

      Press Next step for the next case.

      Do the four cases in order: A, B, C, D.


      Export saves your measurements

      as a CSV file.

      <color=#9AA7B5>Export before you close the page.</color>'
  - title: <b>FINISH THE LAB</b>
    body: 'When all four cases are recorded,

      press Finish on the left screen.


      <color=#FFD54F><b>The timer</b></color>

      It counts down from 2:50:00.

      At 0:00:00 the lab ends by itself.

      <color=#9AA7B5>It turns orange for the last 10 minutes.</color>'
  titleLabel: {fileID: 112250560}
  bodyLabel: {fileID: 1283466080}
  pageLabel: {fileID: 1565083598}
  previousButton: {fileID: 1664127393}
  nextButton: {fileID: 333469454}
