--- !u!114 &1528375140
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1528375138}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 6ed1154995f8e334cabbeb5799cf4642, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::PhysicsLab.Lab.GuideBoard
  pages:
  - title: <b>PRACTICE BENCH</b>
    body: 'This bench is a copy of the lab bench.

      Nothing you do here is recorded or marked.

      Practice as long as you like.


      <color=#FFD54F><b>Press the buttons below</b></color>

      Computer: aim at the button, then click.

      Headset: point at it, squeeze the grip.

      <color=#9AA7B5>Next goes forward. Previous goes back.</color>'
  - title: <b>1   MOVE AND LOOK</b>
    body: '<color=#FFD54F><b>Headset</b></color>

      Look around: turn your head.

      Walk: push the LEFT stick.

      Turn: push the RIGHT stick sideways.

      <color=#FFD54F><b>Computer</b></color>

      First, click the scene once.

      Look: move the mouse. Walk: W, A, S, D.

      Use the buttons on screen: press Tab.

      <color=#9AA7B5>Feel dizzy? Stop and take the headset off.</color>'
  - title: <b>2   GRAB AND LET GO</b>
    body: '<color=#FFD54F><b>Headset</b></color>

      Grab: squeeze the side button (grip).

      Let go: release the grip.

      <color=#FFD54F><b>Computer</b></color>

      Grab: hold the left mouse button on a part.

      Push or pull it: roll the mouse wheel.

      Let go: release the mouse button.

      <color=#9AA7B5>Try it: pick up a mass and put it down.</color>'
  - title: <b>3   HANG A MASS</b>
    body: 'Pick up a mass from the bench.

      Carry it to the small dark loop under a pulley.

      Let go within 10 cm of the loop.

      The mass hangs on the loop.

      Grab it again to take it off.

      <color=#FFD54F><b>150 g needs two masses</b></color>

      Hang 100 g and 50 g on the same loop.

      <color=#9AA7B5>One loop holds up to 4 masses.</color>'
  - title: <b>4   MOVE A PULLEY</b>
    body: 'Grab a pulley. Glowing spots show on the rim.

      The spots are 5 degrees apart.

      Let go within 10 cm of a spot.

      The pulley snaps on and clamps.

      Read its angle on the numbers on the table.

      <color=#9AA7B5>A number shows every 30 degrees.</color>


      <color=#FFD54F><b>Try it: clamp a pulley at 30 degrees</b></color>'
  - title: <b>5   THE SPRING SCALE</b>
    body: 'Grab the spring scale.

      Pull it away from the ring.

      The string pulls the ring along.

      Keep pulling until the ring sits on the post.

      Hold still. The scale shows the force in N.

      <color=#9AA7B5>Let go and it reads 0 N, like a real scale.</color>


      <color=#FFD54F><b>Try it: put the ring on the centre post</b></color>'
  - title: <b>READY FOR THE LAB?</b>
    body: 'Walk to the lab bench next to this one.

      Its board shows the steps and the four cases.


      <color=#FFD54F><b>The timer</b></color>

      The lab time counts down on the left screen.

      Press Finish there when you are done.

      <color=#9AA7B5>The time already runs while you practice.</color>'
  titleLabel: {fileID: 2075592558}
  bodyLabel: {fileID: 1667523552}
  pageLabel: {fileID: 1513675016}
  previousButton: {fileID: 1081081068}
  nextButton: {fileID: 25631837}
